# Adding a package

File: catalog/docs/ADDING.oot

A catalog package is a folder, not a GitHub search result.

1. Create `<name>/manifest` with `name`, `version`, `caps`,
   `deps`, `license`, `payload`, and `sha256` of the payload.
2. Put the payload next to it. Default name is `<name>.oo`.
   The payload needs Academy headers (`// # `, `// Logline:`).
3. Caps must be the real set. opm refuses extra caps on add.
4. From the opm repo, run `opm bot` with this tree as the target.
   That verifies each folder and rewrites `catalog` and `index`.
5. Sign `catalog` to `index.minisig` with the catalog minisign
   secret. Keep the secret out of git.
6. Commit the folder, `catalog`, `index`, and `index.minisig`.
   Push `main`. Pages publishes the files. Auto-release tags.

Do not add a shell recipe. Do not point `opm` at a raw GitHub
tree as the catalog. Git ingest (`origin=git`) is a different
path: pin a commit, then lock. Search reads this file tree.
